# Jott Translator

**Authors: Teju Rajbabu, Kifekachukwu Nwosu, Alvin Jiang, Jiayi Huang, Matthew Gleich**

Phase 1 implements the Jott Tokenizer, responsible for converting a .jott source file into a sequence of tokens based
on the DFA provided in the project specification. The tokenizer was fully completed, compiled, and tested by all group members.

Phase 2 implements the Jott Parser. This takes in a list of tokens and verify the syntax layer of Jott.
The Parser was fully completed, compiled, and tested by all group members.

This project requires JDK 18 or higher to compile and run. This should be checked before compilation with
java -version and javac -version. Environment variables should also include the path to the JDK bin directory.

This should compile the project:
javac Jott.java Nodes/*.java provided/*.java

This should run the project:
java Jott <input.jott> <output_file> <target_language>

See "How to Run" below for the target languages and for building the testers.

This has been tested by all members.

As expected of the project structure:
The provided package should be a top-level package in the src/ folder.

The tester classes (Jott PaserTester and JottTokenizerTester), should be in a package named testers.

The testCases directory should be located in the project's working directory.

Phase 1: All test cases ran successfully with 12/12 passed.
Project tested with other samples in own environments and confirmed by individual contributors.
Project was tested on cs servers and is confirmed to run successfully with no errors.

Phase 2: All test cases ran successfully with 30/30 passed.
Project was tested on cs servers and is confirmed to run successfully with no errors.

Phase 3 implements semantic analysis for Jott.
The parse tree is validated using validateTree() methods implemented throughout the node classes.
Semantic checks include undefined variables/functions, invalid type assignments, incorrect function parameters, missing return statements, uninitialized variables,
and other semantic rules specified in the project description.
Jott.java was also implemented as the main driver for tokenizing, parsing, and semantic validation.

Phase 4 implements code generation. The convertToJott(), convertToJava(), convertToC(), and convertToPython()
methods are implemented throughout the node classes, so a validated tree is translated to Jott, Java, C, or
Python and written to the requested output file. A program is only translated after tokenizing, parsing, and
semantic validation all succeed; an invalid program reports its error and writes no output file.

### How to Run

#### IDE (VS Code/Eclipse)

Run `Jott.java` and provide the following program arguments:

<input.jott> <output_file> <target_language>

Example:

phase3testcases/funcNotDefined.jott output.java Java

#### Terminal

Compile the project:

javac Jott.java Nodes/*.java provided/*.java

Run the translator, where <target_language> is one of Jott, Java, C, or Python:

java Jott <input.jott> <output_file> <target_language>

Examples:

java Jott foo.jott new.jott Jott
java Jott foo.jott NewJott.java Java
java Jott foo.jott new.c C
java Jott foo.jott new.python Python

Giving the same file name for input and output overwrites the original.

To compile and run the generated code:

javac NewJott.java && java NewJott
gcc -o new new.c && ./new
python3 new.python

To compile and run the testers:

javac Jott.java Nodes/*.java provided/*.java testers/*.java
java testers.JottTokenizerTester
java testers.JottParserTester
java testers.JottSemanticTester
java testers.JottPhase4Tester

Each tester expects its test case directory (tokenizerTestCases, parserTestCases, phase3testcases,
phase4testcases) to be in the working directory the tester is run from.

Phase 3: All test cases ran successfully with 63/63 passed.

Phase 4: All test cases ran successfully with 20/20 passed.
Every Phase 4 test program was additionally translated to Java, C, and Python, compiled with javac and gcc,
and run; all three produce identical output for every program.

No external libraries were used in the project.
